<br /> Rhiannon<br /> <br /> Yoruba:<br /> Abata<br /> Aganju<br /> Aje Smaluga<br /> Erinle<br /> Eshu<br /> Gbonka<br /> Gun<br /> Ibeji<br /> Iwa<br /> Jakuta<br /> Moremi<br /> Oba<br /> Obatala<br /> Oduduwa<br /> Olokun<br /> Orisha-Oko<br /> Orungan<br /> Orunmila<br /> Oshosi<br /> Oshumare<br /> Oshun<br /> Oya<br /> Sapona<br /> Timi<br /> Yemanja<br /> <br /> Zapotec:<br /> Cocijo<br /> Coquebila<br /> Coqui Xee<br /> Huechaana<br /> Ndan<br /> Pixee Pecala<br /> <br /> Zulu:<br /> Inkosazana<br /> Intulo<br /> Mamlambo<br /> Mbaba Mwana Waresa<br /> Nokhubulwane<br /> Tikoloshe<br /> Uhlakanyana<br /> Ukqili<br /> Umvelinqangi<br /> Unkulunkulu<br /> Unwaba<br /> Uthlanga<br /> <br /> Other:<br /> Adroa<br /> Ai Apaeac<br /> Baphomet<br /> Kaang<br /> Maushop<br /> Serapis<br /> Sinaa<br /> Wayland<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 11-13-2017, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T15:55:05-07:00","id":1105539,"title":"","content":"Not sure if your looking for any additions, but sense they can be tricky to research online, if you want to expand the Cherokee a bit you can add Sutalidihi (the sun), Geyaguga (the moon), Kana'ti (the lucky hunter) and Selu (corn).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T17:58:21-07:00","id":1105563,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Cherokee suggestions!<br /> Made some edits. Expanded the Hittite, Korean, Iroquios and Cherokee pantheons and made heavy revisions to the Polynesian, with Samoan and Bellona Island pantheons now split out. Separated the Navajo from the Pueblo/Hopi, since they really deserve to be there own pantheon and I'd always intended for them to be, I only just found the proper info to make them so. Added the Vietnamese, Bunyoro, Navajo, Malagasy, Choctaw, Tupari, Muscogee, Ainu, and Nyanga pantheons. <br /> <br /> There's a couple more pantheons I'd like to add, but I can't find enough info for. The Haida most notably, and anything from South America, such as the Chilote. I'm also aware that the Siberian and Aboriginal &quot;pantheons&quot; really should be several pantheons each, but I'm not really sure where to begin in terms of determining how to divide them up. So if anyone has advice in terms of any of that I'm all ears.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'd love suggestions, either for new pantheons or new additions to existing pantheons. My only request is that if you do suggest a new pantheon, I'd like a source, preferably a reliable one, provided for it. Pretty much anything I haven't covered yet is bound to be pretty obscure, except for the Buddhist which I'll get to eventually. I'm also going to add a non-Wabanaki specific Algonquian pantheon, but I'd like to see the official write-up for it first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T18:32:46-07:00","id":1105566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1105563#post1105563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple more pantheons I'd like to add, but I can't find enough info for. The Haida most notably, and anything from South America, such as the Chilote. I'm also aware that the Siberian and Aboriginal &quot;pantheons&quot; really should be several pantheons each, but I'm not really sure where to begin in terms of determining how to divide them up. So if anyone has advice in terms of any of that I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an entire Pantheon list for the Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s, the Haida Pantheon. Just worked on it today, they should be capable of being represented in Scion without any changes or anything, they should be good at the end!<br /> <br /> The figure that frequently gets simply called Raven is normally named Xhuuya, NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas, W\u012b\u2019g\u00eet, The One Of Whom We Speak, and others. Xhuuya is a good 'core' name for him, the extra names are a reflection of Haida culture having a slightly different naming system than you might encounter in some other cultures.<br /> <br /> Ta\u2019\u00f1gwan l\u0101\u2019na is the name of the preeminent being of the tsaran x\u00e0aydaraay, the Sea-People. Sraana guud hiilng7waas is the preeminent being of the Hlk\u2019yaans x\u00e0aydaraay, the Forest-People. There are an abundant numbers of beings who fit here, something like Lesser Gods, but there are a whole host of other figures substantial enough to be Major Gods or Titans. Sk\u00eel dj\u0101\u2019ada-i, Property-Woman, brings wealth, both material and otherwise to people who manage to interact with her somehow. Watghadagaang is a master carver, <i>the</i> master carver, capable of amazing feats of carpentry as well as fighting the Southeast Wind, Xe-\u016b to force the weather to be more stable. Sea-Foam-Woman (I can't, for the life of me, find a traditional spelling of her name) is the ancestress of the raven family, where Djila\u2019qons is the ancestress of the eagle family. Q\u014d\u2019yagiagA\u2019ndal holds up Haida Gwaii beneath the sea after intense strength training.<br /> <br /> And then there are a host of other possibilities for Titans, and whatnot. They are a very interesting, and totally viable Pantheon. I look forward to getting them all set up for Scion 2e!<br /> <br /> If you are looking for advice on ow to break things up, I would do it based on the cultures themselves. Does group X feel that they are different religiously from group Y? Then break their Pantheons up, even if they are very similar to each other. It's how I try to be as respectful as possible to the various cultures I look at for Scion.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the sources for the Haida. A good core is to check out Contributions to the Ethnology of the Haida by J. R. Swanton. An early ethnographic work on the Haida, really quite well done honestly. For more recent works, A Story As Sharp As A Knife: The Classical Haida Mythtellers And Their World by Robert Bringhurst, and Nine Visits to the Mythworld which is a collection of works by Ghandl of the Qayahl Llaanas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-19-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T18:42:59-07:00","id":1105567,"title":"","content":"As for Nanabozo, I'd be extremely surprised if he wasn't a core member of the Manitou in 2e Hero. He slots quite easily into an Anishinaabe pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T20:04:34-07:00","id":1105577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1105566#post1105566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have an entire Pantheon list for the Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s, the Haida Pantheon. Just worked on it today, they should be capable of being represented in Scion without any changes or anything, they should be good at the end!<br /> <br /> The figure that frequently gets simply called Raven is normally named Xhuuya, NA\u00f1k\u00ee\u2019lsLas, W\u012b\u2019g\u00eet, The One Of Whom We Speak, and others. Xhuuya is a good 'core' name for him, the extra names are a reflection of Haida culture having a slightly different naming system than you might encounter in some other cultures.<br /> <br /> Ta\u2019\u00f1gwan l\u0101\u2019na is the name of the preeminent being of the tsaran x\u00e0aydaraay, the Sea-People. Sraana guud hiilng7waas is the preeminent being of the Hlk\u2019yaans x\u00e0aydaraay, the Forest-People. There are an abundant numbers of beings who fit here, something like Lesser Gods, but there are a whole host of other figures substantial enough to be Major Gods or Titans. Sk\u00eel dj\u0101\u2019ada-i, Property-Woman, brings wealth, both material and otherwise to people who manage to interact with her somehow. Watghadagaang is a master carver, <i>the</i> master carver, capable of amazing feats of carpentry as well as fighting the Southeast Wind, Xe-\u016b to force the weather to be more stable. Sea-Foam-Woman (I can't, for the life of me, find a traditional spelling of her name) is the ancestress of the raven family, where Djila\u2019qons is the ancestress of the eagle family. Q\u014d\u2019yagiagA\u2019ndal holds up Haida Gwaii beneath the sea after intense strength training.<br /> <br /> And then there are a host of other possibilities for Titans, and whatnot. They are a very interesting, and totally viable Pantheon. I look forward to getting them all set up for Scion 2e!<br /> <br /> If you are looking for advice on ow to break things up, I would do it based on the cultures themselves. Does group X feel that they are different religiously from group Y? Then break their Pantheons up, even if they are very similar to each other. It's how I try to be as respectful as possible to the various cultures I look at for Scion.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the sources for the Haida. A good core is to check out Contributions to the Ethnology of the Haida by J. R. Swanton. An early ethnographic work on the Haida, really quite well done honestly. For more recent works, A Story As Sharp As A Knife: The Classical Haida Mythtellers And Their World by Robert Bringhurst, and Nine Visits to the Mythworld which is a collection of works by Ghandl of the Qayahl Llaanas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much for the advice with the Haida, and I look forward to seeing your write-up for them!<br /> <br /> Watcher, it seems like there are quite a few lesser-known pantheons you're planning on writing up and have researched heavily, like this and the Abosom. If you don't mind me asking, what are all the pantheons you've selected? I'm pretty curious and I look forward to seeing them.<br /> <br /> I'll look into the Anishinaabe pantheon as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T20:16:58-07:00","id":1105580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1105577#post1105577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks so much for the advice with the Haida, and I look forward to seeing your write-up for them!<br /> <br /> Watcher, it seems like there are quite a few lesser-known pantheons you're planning on writing up and have researched heavily, like this and the Abosom. If you don't mind me asking, what are all the pantheons you've selected? I'm pretty curious and I look forward to seeing them.<br /> <br /> I'll look into the Anishinaabe pantheon as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment, I have done work on the Hittites, the Ashanti, the Haida, and Sacerdos is playing with the Manchu. All four of them should be a lot of fun for all of you hopefully! We are intentionally trying to expand in regions or topics that Scion has traditionally not touched on. The Hittites are possibly the most 'antagonistic to humanity' Pantheon and thus should present fun stories for their Scions trying to mediate the relationship. (Not counting the Irish since, while they don't like their mortals, the Irish can't really <i>do</i> anything about it, while the Hittites frequently bring humanity to the brink of extinction) The Ashanti have a Supreme God, and have a pretty much benevolent cosmology which would give Storytellers unique ways to explore stories. The Haida are a Pantheon that has a <i>very</i> distant semi-Supreme God, as well as having an interesting reciprocal relationship between divine and mortal which should present fun storytelling opportunities. The Manchu, well, they're not my expertise, but they are almost all Goddesses, I think there was only one God in the Major Deities list.<br /> <br /> I am glad you are looking forward to seeing them as well! I really look forward to giving them to you all, I hope they will be enjoyed by people. They have, in the very least, given me a method to better my knowledge of non-European religions which has been a joy for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T07:37:32-07:00","id":1105684,"title":"","content":"That's really awesome Watcher! I'm really looking forward to seeing them. I think they'll provide something unique to the game. I don't know anything about the Manchu pantheon.<br /> <br /> I added a small, tentative Manitou based on a few deities I found on the Native Languages website. I'll revise it heavily when the preview comes out, but at least I have Chibiabos now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T11:14:48-07:00","id":1105775,"title":"","content":"Nanabozo and Cheeby-aub-oozoo have two older brothers, Maudjee-kawiss and Pukawiss. There's also their father Ae-pungishimook (and perhaps their mother Winonah, though I'm uncertain as to whether she'd count), the sky woman Geezhigo-quae, and the earth woman Muzzu-kummik-quae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T12:22:32-07:00","id":1105800,"title":"","content":"Thanks Center-of-All! That's really helpful!<br /> <br /> Okay, I've got another one: Who are the most important of the Palas/Buddhist pantheon? I've kind of got the opposite problem here. Googling them gives me huge lists and I'm struggling to determine who the important ones who would be worthy of inclusion would be. Preferably ones that would be considered gods or at least titans by Scion's definitions, there seems to be a lot of overdeities and varying power levels and I'm not really looking for primordials at the moment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Added the Balinese and updated the Manitou with Center-of-All's suggestions, as well as the Inuit.<br /> Should I be focusing on the Bodhisattvas for the Buddhists?<br /> Also, can anyone think of any more pantheons they'd like to see me add?<br /> <br /> Edit again:<br /> Added a seperate Germanic pantheon, the Guanche, the Mbuti, the Muisca, the Tupari, and the Visayan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 06-20-2017, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T23:24:43-07:00","id":1105962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1105800#post1105800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Center-of-All! That's really helpful!<br /> <br /> Okay, I've got another one: Who are the most important of the Palas/Buddhist pantheon? I've kind of got the opposite problem here. Googling them gives me huge lists and I'm struggling to determine who the important ones who would be worthy of inclusion would be. Preferably ones that would be considered gods or at least titans by Scion's definitions, there seems to be a lot of overdeities and varying power levels and I'm not really looking for primordials at the moment.<br /> <br /> Edit: Added the Balinese and updated the Manitou with Center-of-All's suggestions, as well as the Inuit.<br /> Should I be focusing on the Bodhisattvas for the Buddhists?<br /> Also, can anyone think of any more pantheons they'd like to see me add?<br /> <br /> Edit again:<br /> Added a seperate Germanic pantheon, the Guanche, the Mbuti, the Muisca, the Tupari, and the Visayan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I outlined possibilities for a Buddhist pantheon here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097948-buddhist-scion?p=1097978#post1097978\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...78#post1097978</a><br /> To summarise (and adding some for the sake of your list), candidates would be the Primordials/Buddhas <b>Shakyamuni</b>, <b>Amitabha</b>, and <b>Vairochana</b>, the Major Gods/Bodhisattvas <b>Avalokiteshvara</b>,<b> Kshitigarbha</b>, <b>Manjushri</b>, <b>Samantabadhra</b>, <b>Tara</b>, and <b>Maitreya</b>, furthermore figures like the Vidyarajas/Wisdom Kings (<b>Achala</b>,<b> Trailokyavijaya</b>,<b> Kundali</b>,<b> Vajrabhairava</b>, <b>Vajrayaksha</b>), the Lokapalas/Heavenly Kings/Directional Guardians (<b>Vaishravana</b>, <b>Virudhaka</b>,<b> Dhritarashtra</b>, <b>Virupaksha</b>), the important Devas (e.g. <b>Shakra</b>, <b>Brahma</b>, <b>Yama</b>), and the Arhats/Students of the Buddha. All are opposed by the Titan <b>Mara</b>. There are of course many more Buddhas and Bodhisattvas, but I tried to limit it to the most important/popular ones here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T02:30:40-07:00","id":1105984,"title":"","content":"Very helpful Sacerdos!<br /> <br /> Well, at this point there really isn't much left in terms of accessible pantheons I haven't covered that I can think of. There's still the Manchu, which I suppose I'll add after Sacerdos covers them.<br /> <br /> Are there any gods anyone would like to see added to any pantheons? Major ones I've omitted or minor ones that are particularly interesting in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T03:12:23-07:00","id":1105992,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Yama's siblings playable someday... Surya does have other children, including Yamuna (also known as the Vedic Yami) and Tapti, Goddesses of the rivers of those names, as well as Shani, sometimes identified as Kala, God of Judgement and Misfortune and the Planet Saturn, whose job it is to judge people in life as Yama judges them in Death. In addition, Shiva and Parvati have a couple of daughters that no one ever mentions... Ashoksundari, whose name literally means &quot;She whose beauty destroys sorrow&quot; was created by Parvati as a companion and is a goddess of Joy usually only worshiped in the western parts of India. She is often considered a loving wife and daughter, and is married to the mortal king Nahusha whose piety was so great he was once chosen to replace Indra... that didn't last long. Shiva's other daughter is Manasa, Goddess of Snakes and Venom, who is primarily worshiped in the eastern parts of India. She's most famous for murdering people until they acknowledge her divinity. There's also Kubera, the God of Wealth, but I believe that he's another Mantle of Vaisravana so you may want to keep him in the Palas as suggested by Sacredos where he seems significantly more important.<br /> <br /> You might also like some of the more obscure but nonetheless interesting Vedic era Gods: Pushan, God of Journeys and Travel, as well as in some hymns Sleight of Hand, and Aranyani, Goddess of Forests. There's also Aditi (&quot;The Unbounded One&quot;) Goddess of the Infinite Sky, who is sometimes identified also one with Earth and Heaven (Dyavaprithvi) and is the mother of Indra and Varuna, amongst others. At least one Vedic Hymn extols her as the Supreme Divinity thusly &quot;Aditi is Heaven, Aditi is Space, Aditi is the Mother, the Father and the Child... Aditi is verily all the Universal Gods, as well as the five classes of Being. All that have Been are Aditi, all that will Be, are Aditi.&quot; There's also Vak, the Goddess of Speech, who gets absorbed into Sarasvati later, who also has a &quot;I am the Supreme Divinity speech. Indra's wife Shachi (better known as Indrani) is another inetersting choice because I've never heard of another Goddess of Jealousy before.<br /> <br /> Finally, my personal favourite of the minor but really interesting Deva is Santoshi, the Goddess of Satisfaction, a daughter of Ganesh. What makes her particularly ineteresting is that Santoshi was more or less made up and brought into the public consciousness by a movie... unlike other Deva who are born of oral stories or written scripture, she's born of celluloid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>Edit: Oh, also Varuni, Goddess of Booze... you can never have enough of those around and I'm sure Dionysus would appreciate the company.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 06-21-2017, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:06:14-07:00","id":1106005,"title":"","content":"Those suggestions sound really interesting Samudra. Thanks a lot! It's good to have the Devas better represented since they are such a large pantheon.<br /> <br /> I think I want to stop at 1500 gods, of which there are 1435 currently, leaving open 65 slots unless I made a mistake and have an undesired double up. I'm not adding any more pantheons at this point, except for the Manchu, I have over 80 and I think that's enough. Still, if anyone has any further suggestions, I'm all ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T05:45:32-07:00","id":1106017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1105984#post1105984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very helpful Sacerdos!<br /> <br /> Well, at this point there really isn't much left in terms of accessible pantheons I haven't covered that I can think of. There's still the Manchu, which I suppose I'll add after Sacerdos covers them.<br /> <br /> Are there any gods anyone would like to see added to any pantheons? Major ones I've omitted or minor ones that are particularly interesting in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Manchu will still take some time - sources on them are scarce in general, and especially scarce in Western languages (most is in Russian and Chinese, neither of which I speak); their religion is difficult, highly localised, and wildly different between the common populace and the shamanic elite. I have a rough outline of a very small pantheon for them right now, I could surely give you the names if nothing else, but that could all still change as I go on reading, and hopefully figure them out somewhat more clearly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But if it's useful to you, a WIP-list of the Major Gods:<br /> <b>Abka Hehe / Abka Enduri</b>: &quot;Sky Woman&quot;, the creator goddess and embodiment of heaven, who, under the latter name, takes on a male form in peaceful times<br /> <b>Banamu Hehe</b>: narcoleptic goddess of the earth, a sister Abka Hehe created for herself<br /> <b>Ulden Hehe</b>: goddess of light, stars, and the sun, a sister Abka Hehe created for herself<br /> <b>Tumu</b>: Goddess of the Fire in the Stones<br /> <b>Omosi Mama</b>: goddess who creates souls, goddess of fertility, patron of shamans, lives in the underworld<br /> <b>Ilmun Khan</b>: ruler of the underworld, form of Yama (not sure if really major)<br /> <b>Golmin Sangiyan Alin</b>: god of the Chang-baishan Mountains, leader of all the gods of natural features (not sure if really major)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":". 06-21-2017, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:16:48-07:00","id":1106038,"title":"","content":"With australian deities, there is also Balayang, Bamapana, Barraiya (definitely required if you have Eingana), Bila, Bunjil, Daramulum, Julunggul (you have a rainbow snake on the list, but the one you listed is one of the only few ones which isn't a rain/fertility tied one), Karora, Kidili, Kunapipi (her thing is basically being a parent to Scions), Mangar-kunjer-kunja, Ngi\u1e49\u1e6faka, and Wandjina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T07:38:13-07:00","id":1106048,"title":"","content":"Updated once again, with the Manchu (thanks again Sacerdos) and Milo's Australian suggestions. I'm very glad for those, by the way. An entire continent with only 14 or so deities to represent it really didn't feel right.<br /> <br /> Edit: 1452 deities. 48 spots left!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 06-21-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:32:38-07:00","id":1106097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1106005#post1106005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those suggestions sound really interesting Samudra. Thanks a lot! It's good to have the Devas better represented since they are such a large pantheon.<br /> <br /> I think I want to stop at 1500 gods, of which there are 1435 currently, leaving open 65 slots unless I made a mistake and have an undesired double up. I'm not adding any more pantheons at this point, except for the Manchu, I have over 80 and I think that's enough. Still, if anyone has any further suggestions, I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, I missed the part up there where you noted that you wanted titan ideas as well as Gods... while you've gotten most of the major Puranic Asura, consider also Vritra, the Vedic Dark Sinuous Dragon who holds the waters of the world within his fortresses until Indra kills him and lets loose the waters into the world (some scholars think he's an embodiment of the dark storm clouds that are split open by lightning (Indra) to make rain, so his Purview would probably be Sky or Chaos). He's a pretty major Vedic era figure, along with the Panis, a tribe of demons who stole the cattle of the world, along with Ushas (who may have been in cow form herself) and sealed them into an underground cavern, from which Indra rescues them, creating the day (their Purviews would probably be Earth or Darkness).<br /> <br /> Puranic era wise, there's Mayasura, also known as MayaDanava (whose name is not pronounced as Maya with the long As, but who is associated with optical illusions) the greatest of Asura architects, who is a surprising presence in the background of Hindu myth... he is Ravana's father-in-law in the Ramayana, and it is he who built the Pandava's palace in the Mahabharata the optical illusions in which helped precipitate the great war in that epic (basically, he built a room in the palace with floor of glass with a pool in between, but it was impossible to tell which floor tile was glass and which was water... and Duryodhana, eldest of the Pandavas antagonistic cousins, fell into the water, and Draupadi, wife of the Pandavas and possible Avatar of Kali depending on who you ask, laughed, and said &quot;there goes the blind son of a blind father&quot; (since Duryodhana's father was blind) which insult eventually helped to precipitate the Kurukshetra war after many more adventures). His Purviews would likely be Forge or Deception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T12:45:55-07:00","id":1106203,"title":"","content":"Thanks again Samudra. I can't believe I forgot Vritra!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T15:09:47-07:00","id":1106277,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any lesser-known Shen they'd like to see? It's a really large pantheon, and some of the more niche members are pretty unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:31:13-07:00","id":1106382,"title":"","content":"Well for the Shen you can always add the eight immortals and the four dragon kings. Aside from them you have Zao Shen, the kitchen god, and Yue Lao the love god. There are obviously more, but I'm by no means all that knowledgeable on Chinese mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T19:54:08-07:00","id":1106389,"title":"","content":"Some deities to add to the awesomeness that is the UDL - The Tarascan Gods of Mexico. I don't have a lot of info on them, but they are different from the Mayans, Aztecs, Zapotecs, et al.<br /> <br /> Chicomecoatl<br /> Chupithiripeme<br /> Cuerauaperi<br /> Curicaueri<br /> Pevame<br /> Querenda-Angapeti<br /> Tihume<br /> Uitzimengari<br /> Xaratanga<br /> <br /> And for the Aztecs:<br /> <br /> Mictecacihuatl, Lady of the Dead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":". 06-21-2017, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T07:54:04-07:00","id":1106545,"title":"","content":"Another Mesoamerican pantheon? Cool! Thanks for the suggestion Purple Snit! Glad you think the list is awesome!<br /> <br /> I did actually have Mictecacihuatl, just under a different spelling. Changed the spelling now, as I assume your version is probably more recognisable.<br /> <br /> Updated once again with the Tarascans, the Four Dragon Kings, the Eight Immortals, a couple other Shen, and a couple more Hindu bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T12:25:48-07:00","id":1111775,"title":"","content":"Been a while since my last revision, but here's a new one. No new pantheons this time, but some more added to existing pantheons, including several potential titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T11:38:34-07:00","id":1112247,"title":"","content":"[bows with respect]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T12:49:59-07:00","id":1112284,"title":"","content":"I know I have a book laying around that describes the Kaftar (Pre-Islamic Afghan) pantheon, but I can't seem to locate it. That will probably be the next pantheon I add when I find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:22:23-07:00","id":1112634,"title":"","content":"Have you thought of adding the deities of ancient Rhodes? They feature in Greek Myth and would make a great fallen pantheon. They're called the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Telchines</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:12:16-07:00","id":1112878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1112634#post1112634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you thought of adding the deities of ancient Rhodes? They feature in Greek Myth and would make a great fallen pantheon. They're called the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Telchines</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> <br /> This is certainly very interesting. I'd always just assumed that the Telchines were just another race of humanoid monsters, albeit a very weird one. I wasn't aware that they were the remnants of a previous pantheon and had actually received worship.<br /> <br /> Still, I think I'd like a little more info on them individually to work with then that. Even the Minoan, Etruscan, Basque, etc. pantheons have some basic information known about the roles of each known deity, so at least they have something to work with.<br /> <br /> Got to say they have really badass sounding names. Chryson, Makelo, <i>Demonax, </i>the names do sound really cool. Perhaps if we had someone who knew the etymology of those names (which I personally do not), that could at least give us a starting point.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I really like the idea of these guys filling the Atlantean pantheon niche. Having an Atlantean-esque pantheon where at least the names originate in mythology sounds a lot better then one where they were just made up, and I like the idea of them being a lost/fallen pantheon destroyed by the Theoi, with all the associated lost civilization tropes and plot points.<br /> <br /> Okay, let me tell you what I'll do. I've been planning a special section at the bottom concerning non-traditional, pseudo-pantheons like an Archangel pantheon, the figures from the Ars Goetia, and a &quot;pantheon&quot; of American folklore figures like a lot of people have been discussing, which would be optionally canon and people could take or leave as they please. I think I'll have these guys fill the Atlantean pantheon role when I do that. Not enough is really known for them to make the main list, but they can certainly be included in a manner such as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T11:23:54-07:00","id":1113299,"title":"","content":"Update time. Added the Dogon and a small number of Ceram. Updated the Zulu, Mapuche, and Aboriginal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:04:32-07:00","id":1116806,"title":"","content":"Update. Fixed some formatting errors, a couple accidental deity double-ups, and added the Burmese pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T12:28:54-07:00","id":1117369,"title":"","content":"A new pantheon to add to the UDL, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jingpo_people#Culture\" target=\"_blank\">Kachin</a> pantheon! They are less integrated into Buddhism than the Burmese nat and retain most of their pre-Buddhist/Christian influences to this day<br /> <br /> Karai Kasang<br /> Samhpwi Nang majan<br /> Woishun<br /> La'n Roi<br /> Madai<br /> Sinlap<br /> Jan Wa<br /> Hkring Wan<br /> Jahka<br /> Jan<br /> Shata<br /> Bunghpoi<br /> 'n Bung<br /> Samwi<br /> Mashawhe<br /> Marang","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:28:21-07:00","id":1117527,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, Svarogg! They're on there now too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T11:12:42-07:00","id":1125284,"title":"","content":"I've decided, in light of the new Netjer preview and the discussion surrounding it, to update my own Netjer list with the proper, original, Egyptian names rather than the Greek ones. The trouble is, other than the ones in the preview, I'm not really sure which names on here are correct and which ones aren't, and what the correct names would be. Help would be greatly appreciated. Here's the list:<br /> Ammit<br /> Amun<br /> Anubis - Anpu<br /> Apep<br /> Ash<br /> Aten<br /> Atum<br /> Babi<br /> Bastet<br /> Bat<br /> Bes<br /> Geb<br /> Hapy<br /> Hathor- Het-Heru<br /> Heka<br /> Heqet<br /> Horus- Heru<br /> Isis- Aset<br /> Khepri<br /> Khnum<br /> Khonsu<br /> Kuk<br /> Ma\u2019at<br /> Mafdet<br /> Meretseger<br /> Min<br /> Mut<br /> Neith<br /> Nekhbet<br /> Nephthys<br /> Nu<br /> Nun<br /> Nut<br /> Osiris- Wesir<br /> Ptah<br /> Ra- Re<br /> Sekhmet<br /> Serket<br /> Seshat<br /> Seth<br /> Shu<br /> Sobek<br /> Tawaret<br /> Tefnut<br /> Thoth- Djehuty<br /> Wadjet<br /> Wepwawet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:25:36-07:00","id":1126847,"title":"","content":"Updated the Netjer. I replaced Bat, who's essentially the same as Het-Heru, with the more interesting Shezmu. I also switched over to the proper, original names, or at least the ones I was aware of. I'm pretty certain the rest are the original names regardless but feel free to correct me if I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T13:08:41-07:00","id":1149769,"title":"","content":"My first update in quite a while! I added the Bicalano pantheon, as well as the solitary Sinaa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:14:48-08:00","id":1158208,"title":"","content":"I made a few minor edits, most notably adding the Miwok pantheon, and a few miscellaneous figures like Adroa, Wayland, and Maushop. By the way, if anyone can point me in the direction of any more Wampanoag deities besides Maushop, it would be greatly appreciated. I know that they follow the &quot;one distant creator&quot; model, but I didn't see anything to indicate that Maushop is the only god-level (rather than primordial-level) entity that exists for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T05:30:16-08:00","id":1158427,"title":"","content":"From<a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/wampanoag-legends.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> this website</a>:<br /> There are three others<ul><li>Squannit, the wife of Maushop and the Sea-Woman</li> <li>Hobomock, the god of death and the adversary of Kehtannit</li> <li>Kehtannit, the Great Spirit</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T16:48:53-08:00","id":1158704,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info! I'll add a small Wampanoag pantheon in the next update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T08:10:09-08:00","id":1158949,"title":"","content":"I'd really love to see Ame-no-Uzume-no-Mikoto on the Japanese list. For the Greek, I'd love Psyche and Hedone. The latter I believe is a daimone, not sure which class &quot;mortal ascended to god hood by marrying Eros&quot; qualifies as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T15:44:26-08:00","id":1159234,"title":"","content":"Will do. Expect them in the next update.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the Theoi I'm considering adding a section for Orphic deities. I'm particularly interested in Zagreus, who according to some sources, might be Hades and Persephone's son.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T17:56:52-08:00","id":1527585,"title":"","content":"I have seen this list, with all the time that has passed, here are several to update and contribute:<br /> <br /> Aboriginal Australian:<br /> Jar Edo Wens don't exist<br /> <br /> Armenian (extra):<br /> Angel<br /> Andndayin Oj<br /> Ayg<br /> Vanatur<br /> <br /> Brasilian Yoruba:<br /> Exu Caveira<br /> Exu Tranca-rua<br /> Maria Padilha<br /> Maria Navalha<br /> Vovo Maria Conga<br /> Ze Pelintra<br /> <br /> Cashinahua:<br /> Chana<br /> Isatawaka<br /> Kana<br /> Manen'inobuena<br /> Nawatete<br /> Shet\u00e9<br /> Yobuenawaboshka<br /> Yotan<br /> <br /> Fang-Beti:<br /> Abo Mama<br /> Akoma Mba<br /> Angoung Bere<br /> Angone Zok<br /> Asseng Mbane<br /> Ayangoum<br /> Bissiga Ndong<br /> Engouang Ondo<br /> Efoua Medang<br /> Ekang Nna<br /> Eyang<br /> Eyo<br /> Mbot Okomo Sala<br /> Mesi Me Kot Endong<br /> Ngu\u00e9ma \u00c9kang<br /> Nguema Nsing Bere<br /> Nkeg Afane Mye<br /> Nkeyeng Assoumou<br /> Ntoutoume Mfoulou<br /> Nze Medang<br /> Nzame<br /> Obame Andome<br /> Obiang Medza<br /> Okome Ekang<br /> Ossimi Ngu\u00e9ma Ekang<br /> Oyono Ada Ngone<br /> Zeyan<br /> Zogo Bikuku<br /> Zong Mebegue<br /> <br /> Gnosticism:<br /> Abraxas<br /> Anthropos<br /> Acinetos<br /> Ageratos<br /> Ainos<br /> Autogenes<br /> Autophyes<br /> Agape<br /> Barbelo<br /> Bythos<br /> Bythios<br /> Ecclesia<br /> Ecclesiasticus<br /> Elpis<br /> Hedone<br /> Henosis<br /> Horos<br /> Logos<br /> Macaria<br /> Macariotes<br /> Mixis<br /> Monad<br /> Nous<br /> Patricas<br /> Pistis<br /> Sige<br /> Sophia<br /> Synesis<br /> Theletus<br /> <br /> Archons:<br /> Adonaios<br /> Astaphaios<br /> Elaios<br /> Horaios<br /> Iao<br /> Sabaoth<br /> Saklas<br /> Yaldabaoth<br /> <br /> Theosophy:<br /> Aiwass<br /> Djwal Khul<br /> Hilarion<br /> Kuthumi<br /> Meta<br /> Morya<br /> Mother Venus<br /> Nada<br /> Paul the Venetian<br /> Poimandries<br /> Saint Germain<br /> Sanat Kumara<br /> Thevetat<br /> <br /> Guarani (note: Pombero isn't a god):<br /> Anhanga<br /> Anhum<br /> Caapor\u00e1<br /> Derekey<br /> Dereveruy<br /> Guarac\u00ed<br /> Jakaira<br /> Jac\u00ed<br /> Jurupari<br /> Nhandessy<br /> Porassy<br /> Tum\u00e9 Arandu<br /> Uiara<br /> <br /> Tau and Sons:<br /> Ao Ao<br /> Jasy Jatere<br /> Kurupi<br /> Luison<br /> Mboi Tui<br /> Monai<br /> Tau<br /> Teju Jagua<br /> <br /> Guarayo:<br /> Abaangui<br /> <br /> Scythian:<br /> Akinaka<br /> Api<br /> Artimpasa<br /> Gaithasura<br /> Papaios<br /> Tapayanti<br /> Targitavah<br /> Thvashamazata<br /> <br /> Venezuelan folklore:<br /> Andres Bello<br /> Don Juan del Tabaco<br /> Don Nicanor Ochoa<br /> Guaicaipuro<br /> Ismael Sanchez<br /> Jose Gregorio<br /> Maria Lionza<br /> Negro Felipe<br /> Simon Bolivar<br /> <br /> Yazidism:<br /> Amadin<br /> Ezdina Mir<br /> Fakhredin<br /> Hevruz<br /> Hesen<br /> Khatuna Fakhra<br /> Kiraz<br /> Melek Taus<br /> Mem Reshan<br /> Mem Sivan<br /> Miseleh<br /> Nasirdin<br /> Mand<br /> Muse Sor<br /> Obekir<br /> Pir Afat<br /> Pire Ewra<br /> Sahsiwar<br /> Sejadin<br /> Sheikh Shams<br /> Sitiya Es<br /> <br /> Zoroastrian (extra):<br /> Drvaspa<br /> Khvarenah<br /> Nairyosangha<br /> Rata","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","user":"PlebSparks","date":". 12-28-2023, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T04:08:05-08:00","id":1528254,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I know a bit about Brazilian mythology, so if you don't mind me helping a bit:<br /> <br /> The Guarani Pantheon presented there is more based on the Nuestros Antepassados, a questionable account of ancient Guarani mythology (which can be found here <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080605015343/http://www.bvp.org.py/biblio_htm/colman/cap01_05.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20080605...n/cap01_05.htm</a>). As far as I understand this source would be as accurate as the Prose Edda or the Lebor Gab\u00e1la Erenn, in the sense that it is a later Christian view of the myths. Either way, we have living Guarani people, so while this can be used as a source, it is not the best to be used as the sole source.<br /> <br /> If I was going to separate them into two pantheons I would do the following:<br /> <br /> <b>Guarani </b>(from Nuestros Antepassados)<br /> Angatupry<br /> Tume Arandu<br /> Por\u00e3ssy<br /> Jacy<br /> Tume Arandu<br /> Tup\u00e3<br /> Tau<br /> <br /> (depending on how you define a god or titan this list can grown longer. I am going for a more basic one)<br /> <br /> <b>Guarani </b>(from more current sources)<br /> Anhum<br /> Caapor\u00e3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nhanderuvu\u00e7u<br /> Tup\u00e3<br /> Jakaira<br /> Nhamandu<br /> Karai<br /> Derekey<br /> Dereveruy<br /> Nhandessy<br /> Aracy<br /> Ruda<br /> Xari\u00e3<br /> <br /> I also would put the <b>Tupi</b> pantheon together, as two of the gods on the list are Tupi gods..<br /> <br /> <b>Tupi</b><br /> Caapor\u00e3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monai<br /> Moire-Monan<br /> Tup\u00e3<br /> Uiara<br /> <br /> To add a few more Brazilian Pantheons<br /> <br /> <b>Kadiweu</b><br /> G\u00f4-no\u00eano-h\u00f4di<br /> G\u00f4-ni\u00e1-juh\u00fad\u200b<br /> Ninigo\u200b<br /> Nibet\u00e1d\u200b</span><br /> <br /> <b>Tukano/Desana</b><br /> \u200bBaaribo<br /> \u200bGuram\u00fcye<br /> \u200bWar\u00e3ri O\u00e3ku<br /> \u200bYamiki Muhipu<br /> \u200bAbe<br /> Amo<br /> Boreka<br /> \u200bDoetiro<br /> Umtikosur\u00e3panami<br /> \u200bThe Dior\u00e1s<br /> \u200bKisibi<br /> Buhtari G\u00f5\u00e3<span style=\"color:#767678\">m</span><b>\u0169</b>\u200b<br /> Deyubari G\u00f5\u00e3<span style=\"color:#767678\">m</span><b>\u0169</b>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I might pass and post a few more later. I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 01-09-2024, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T09:06:57-08:00","id":1528263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1528254#post1528254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tukano/Desana</b><br /> Baaribo<br /> Guram\u00fcye<br /> \u200bWar\u00e3ri O\u00e3ku<br /> \u200bYamiki Muhipu<br /> \u200bAbe<br /> Amo<br /> Boreka<br /> \u200bDoetiro<br /> Umtikosur\u00e3panami<br /> \u200bThe Dior\u00e1s<br /> \u200bKisibi<br /> Buhtari G\u00f5\u00e3<span style=\"color:#767678\">m</span><b>\u0169</b>\u200b<br /> Deyubari G\u00f5\u00e3<span style=\"color:#767678\">m</span><b>\u0169</b>\u200b\u200b<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>From my own research, I read that the Desana had no gods. What is their concept of superior beings?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T09:19:58-08:00","id":1528265,"title":"","content":"Getting back to that, the Cherokee pantheon also needs to be updated. With the deities noted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28198-ahisgewaya\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28198_2.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28198\" data-vbnamecard=\"28198\">Ahisgewaya</a> in his fan concept<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1522782-new-tsalagi-cherokee-pantheon-or-just-more-manitou-for-scion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1522782-new-tsalagi-cherokee-pantheon-or-just-more-manitou-for-scion\"> New Tsalagi (Cherokee) pantheon, or just more Manitou for Scion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1522782-new-tsalagi-cherokee-pantheon-or-just-more-manitou-for-scion\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1522782-new-tsalagi-cherokee-pantheon-or-just-more-manitou-for-scion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I am a Cherokee and have studied our religion for quite a while. I made a pantheon using this, although there are a lot of similarities to the Manitou. Anyone has my official permission to use this in their Scion games. The letter &amp;quot;v&amp;quot; in Tsalagi is pronounced &amp;quot;uh&amp;quot; and the TS is kind of like a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Cherokee (extra)<br /> Asgaya Gigagei<br /> D\u00e2yuni's\u00ef<br /> Eduda Suli<br /> Inage Utasuhi<br /> Jistu<br /> Kanati<br /> Ocasta<br /> Unetlanvhi<br /> U\u2019tlun\u2019ta","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T00:57:12-08:00","id":1528309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlebSparks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1528263#post1528263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my own research, I read that the Desana had no gods. What is their concept of superior beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wanting to enter into the question of &quot;What are gods&quot;, these beings are usually beings that did great deeds, typically guiding spirits to their transformation to humans (and animals, varying from the version), and help to organize the World as it is, creating stuff like the Cassava (main food staple), rituals, and even the women as they are. More typically they are called demiurges.<br /> <br /> The most obvious superior being of them is Yeba Belo, the Great Grandmother of the Universe, a primordial who created the bases of the cosmos and the Thunders who started to create the world but never finished, followed by the Umtikosur\u00e3panami (aka. \u00cbm\u00ebko Sul\u00e3n Pal\u00e3min), the Great Grandson of the Universe, who finished the job. After that, some other great beings were created (Baaribo, Deyubari G\u00f5\u00e3m\u0169\u200b\u200b\u200b, \u200bWar\u00e3ri O\u00e3ku, etc.) who, while created with humans, had knowledge, power, and responsibilities beyond those, and would later create many of the rituals characteristics of the World, face terrible foes, and typically ended by dancing and rising into the sky to live there.<br /> <br /> These names are not all Desana names for the gods, as they are very much shared by the Tukano peoples, so it is a mix of both.<br /> <br /> As far as I could get (and I admit right now I am a bit behind on that knowledge) the Desana do not pray towards these beings, acting more with the rituals and prayers they created/taught to them. I don't know where you saw that Desana does not have gods, but maybe it is specific to one group of the Desana (as they are very varied) or they just don't consider these beings as gods <i>per se.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T14:55:45-08:00","id":1528341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1528309#post1528309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not wanting to enter into the question of &quot;What are gods&quot;, these beings are usually beings that did great deeds, typically guiding spirits to their transformation to humans (and animals, varying from the version), and help to organize the World as it is, creating stuff like the Cassava (main food staple), rituals, and even the women as they are. More typically they are called demiurges.<br /> <br /> The most obvious superior being of them is Yeba Belo, the Great Grandmother of the Universe, a primordial who created the bases of the cosmos and the Thunders who started to create the world but never finished, followed by the Umtikosur\u00e3panami (aka. \u00cbm\u00ebko Sul\u00e3n Pal\u00e3min), the Great Grandson of the Universe, who finished the job. After that, some other great beings were created (Baaribo, Deyubari G\u00f5\u00e3m\u0169\u200b\u200b, \u200bWar\u00e3ri O\u00e3ku, etc.) who, while created with humans, had knowledge, power, and responsibilities beyond those, and would later create many of the rituals characteristics of the World, face terrible foes, and typically ended by dancing and rising into the sky to live there.<br /> <br /> These names are not all Desana names for the gods, as they are very much shared by the Tukano peoples, so it is a mix of both.<br /> <br /> As far as I could get (and I admit right now I am a bit behind on that knowledge) the Desana do not pray towards these beings, acting more with the rituals and prayers they created/taught to them. I don't know where you saw that Desana does not have gods, but maybe it is specific to one group of the Desana (as they are very varied) or they just don't consider these beings as gods <i>per se.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Scion includes some other pantheons whose members don't consider themselves gods--there's the Orisha of the Yoruba and the Yazatas of Persia at the very least and there may be more I'm not remembering. It sounds like at least some of these beings that the Desana honor would qualify as gods in game-mechanical terms, even if they don't consider themselves gods, the same as the Orisha and Yazatas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T16:46:26-08:00","id":1528344,"title":"","content":"If we treat the Angels and Saints as a Pantheon, they wouldn't call themselves gods either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:18:31-08:00","id":1528600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1528344#post1528344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we treat the Angels and Saints as a Pantheon, they wouldn't call themselves gods either.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, although I don't think of the saints as a pantheon.<br /> Even taking the most &quot;powerful&quot; ones like Saint Peter or Saint George, seeing them do things like gods is rare and contradicts the idea that they are humans, not enlightened or &quot;ascended&quot; humans, simply men who felt more faith in the Almighty than the majority.<br /> Different thing with Orisha where in their own stories it is seen that they are still different from humans even if they are not The God","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:44:00-08:00","id":1528604,"title":"","content":"Agreed. IMHO, Legend is a bad fit for the Abrahamic religions; a variant of Awareness (from Masks of the Mythos) works better for their holy men, while a variation of Heritage (from Dragon) works better for angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:45:38-08:00","id":1530178,"title":"","content":"I made 4 lists of fictional pantheons (Lovecraft Circle, Dunsany, William Blake and Clark Ashton Smith) and the list of angels and demons.<br /> For the Abrahamic I was quite permissive, also canonizing the Ars Goetia, its counterpart the Shem HaMephorash and some figures from Paradise Lost and Visio Tnugdali.<br /> <br /> Abrahamic:<br /> Achaiah<br /> Aladiah<br /> Anavel<br /> Aniel<br /> Ariel<br /> Asaliah<br /> Azrael<br /> Cahethel<br /> Caliel<br /> Chavakiah<br /> Damabiah<br /> Daniel<br /> Eiael<br /> Elemiah<br /> Gabriel<br /> Haaiah<br /> Haamiah<br /> Habuiah<br /> Hahahel<br /> Hahaiah<br /> Hahasiah<br /> Haiaiel<br /> Haiviah<br /> Hakamiah<br /> Haniel<br /> Harahel<br /> Hariel<br /> Haziel<br /> Iahhael<br /> Iehahel<br /> Iehuiah<br /> Ieiaiel<br /> Ieialel<br /> Ieiazel<br /> Ielahiah<br /> Ielial<br /> Ierathel<br /> Iezalel<br /> Imamiah<br /> Israfil<br /> Kafniel<br /> Laviah<br /> Lecabel<br /> Lehahiah<br /> Levuiah<br /> Loviah<br /> Mahasiah<br /> Manadel<br /> Mavakel<br /> Mebahaiah<br /> Mebahel<br /> Mehiel<br /> Melahel<br /> Metatron<br /> Michael<br /> Mihael<br /> Mizrael<br /> Moroni<br /> Mumiah<br /> Munkar<br /> M\u00e1lik<br /> Nanael<br /> Nelchael<br /> Nemamiah<br /> Nithael<br /> Nithhaiah<br /> Omael<br /> Osrail<br /> Pahaliah<br /> Poiel<br /> Rakib<br /> Ramiel<br /> Raziel<br /> Rehael<br /> Reiaiel<br /> Roehel<br /> Saeehiah<br /> Samael<br /> Sealiah<br /> Sitael<br /> Uriel<br /> Vasariah<br /> Vehuel<br /> Vehuiah<br /> Veualiah<br /> Vmabel<br /> Yabamiah<br /> Zatchiel<br /> <br /> Beasts:<br /> Acheron<br /> Behemot<br /> Leviathan<br /> Therion<br /> Ziz<br /> <br /> Grigori:<br /> Ananel<br /> Araqiel<br /> Armumahel<br /> Arteqoph<br /> Asael<br /> Azazel<br /> Baraqel<br /> Bezaliel<br /> Chazaqiel<br /> D