> Sish<br /> Skarl<br /> Slid<br /> Trehagobol<br /> The Evening<br /> Triboogie<br /> Umborodom<br /> Wohoon<br /> Yoharneth-Lahai<br /> Zanes<br /> Zeebol<br /> Zodrak<br /> <br /> William Blake (fic):<br /> Ahania<br /> Albion<br /> Bromion<br /> Enion<br /> Enitharmon<br /> Luvah<br /> Palamabron<br /> Rintrah<br /> Tharmas<br /> Theotormon<br /> Urizen<br /> Urthona<br /> Vala<br /> \u200b<br /> Zothique (fic):<br /> Basatan<br /> Geol<br /> Mordiggian<br /> Ojhal<br /> Thamagorgos<br /> Thasaidon<br /> Vergama<br /> Yucla<br /> Yulul\u00fan\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> I really like the mythopoeia pantheons, although the only 4 for public use that I find with these, are there more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","user":"PlebSparks","date":". 04-30-2024, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T11:39:59-08:00","id":1530464,"title":"","content":"I made an update to the list of Circassian gods (aside from making it Circassian-Ossetian because they share the same folklore)<br /> Circassian-Ossetian:<br /> Afsati<br /> Aminon<br /> Barastyr<br /> Donbettir<br /> Falvar<br /> Galagon<br /> Huyaendon Aelder<br /> Kurdalaegon<br /> Saubarag<br /> Safa<br /> Tutyr<br /> Uastyrdzhi<br /> Uacilla<br /> Xwycau<br /> <br /> Narts:<br /> Akhsar<br /> Akhsartag<br /> Bartraz<br /> Dzerassae<br /> Haemyts<br /> Pizighash<br /> Pkharmat<br /> Satanaya<br /> Sosruquo<br /> Syrdon<br /> Tlepsh<br /> Uryzmaeg<br /> Warzameg<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, what treatment would the Narts receive if this pantheon were designed? The Nart sagas and the cosmology around them are not mythology; they are mythopoeia, like the Tuatha d\u00e9 Danann. But unlike them, the Nart are NOT the gods that people worship; those would be the Dzuar (the first list). They are just like the &quot;main characters&quot; of the sagas. Would it be a Circassian pantheon with the Nart subpantheon attached from the beginning? I was also thinking about incomplete mantles like Camelot in Once and Future, but the Narts are canonically divine (They are all children of Satanaya, who is also the daughter of the Dzuar Uastyrdzhi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","user":"PlebSparks","date":". 02-10-2024, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T13:16:54-08:00","id":1530471,"title":"","content":"Certain Saints, Bridget comes to mind, are pagan gods brought into a Christian worldview by making them Saints. A list of &quot;Saints&quot; that are Mantels of gods would be useful. It would give an idea of were some gods might have unexpected power/influence in the world. <br /> <br /> Also, a popular Saint that is the Mantel for more than one god, is a great point of conflict. Both Bride and Oya would want to control the Mantel of Saint Bridget. How would that fight go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-18T07:10:07-07:00","id":1534393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlebSparks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1105409-ultimate-deity-list-wip?p=1530178#post1530178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made 4 lists of fictional pantheons (Lovecraft Circle, Dunsany, William Blake and Clark Ashton Smith) and the list of angels and demons.<br /> For the Abrahamic I was quite permissive, also canonizing the Ars Goetia, its counterpart the Shem HaMephorash and some figures from Paradise Lost and Visio Tnugdali.<br /> <br /> Abrahamic:<br /> <br /> Pegana (fic):<br /> Dorozhand<br /> Eimes<br /> Gribaun<br /> Habaniah<br /> Hish<br /> Hoodrazai<br /> Inzana<br /> Limpang-Tung<br /> Kib<br /> Mana Yood Sushai<br /> Mung<br /> Ranorada<br /> Roon<br /> Segastrion<br /> Sish<br /> Skarl<br /> Slid<br /> Trehagobol<br /> The Evening<br /> Triboogie<br /> Umborodom<br /> Wohoon<br /> Yoharneth-Lahai<br /> Zanes<br /> Zeebol<br /> Zodrak<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I missed some gods, here's an update:<br /> <br /> Pegana (fic):<br /> Sirami - The god of oblivion who sits at the end of the milky way<br /> The North Wind - Another unnamed god, he was sent by Inzana to recover the sun from the cloud gods.<br /> Tintaggon - The god of the black marble mountain, who was able to confront Slid in his conquest of surface lands.<br /> Trogool - The primordial god who turns the pages of the book where the days and nights pass<br /> Umbool - God of drought who is subordinate to Mung, used by the latter to put the river gods Eimes, Zanes and Segastrion in their place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28200-plebsparks","name":"PlebSparks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28200_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}